  "body": "The AC path solver returns the source move index on success, but not when a move exceeds rotary travel. In an offline test of the native solver at [`4e7929dfe4`](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/tree/4e7929dfe4b5bae9d1f5154e8e48c40e675d8b1c/crates/post/src/kinematics), the same unreachable orientation on move 0 and move 2 produced identical C-axis errors. The caller could not tell which move to inspect.\n\n**Done means:** The caller can identify the original move index for both refusals. Keep the axis, required angle, and travel limits in the error. Add a regression test. Do not change which moves the solver accepts or the output it generates. This does not implement the post integration in #1969.\n\nSuggested labels: `P7`, `effort:medium`, `area:post`, `area:multiaxis`, `source:agent`.",
